    "Up-classification requires captured PostgreSQL 17.4 catalog evidence profile 17-v3 and an explicitly migrated core 0.3.0 Field; modified captures require recapture. Raw DDL alone does not establish stored-relation guarantees.",
    "Only ordinary/partitioned stored-relation values under explicit SQL-NULL policy are classified; query-output and omitted-input semantics remain distinct.",
    "A false notNull flag alone is insufficient; domains, constraints, generated fields, unresolved triggers and unknown refinements remain residual or blocked. No arbitrary native expression evaluation is claimed.",
    "Classification retains complete native captures and scope extensions; existing author intent and binding metadata cannot be overwritten silently.",
    "Authored projection supports one Field and the 14 existing pg_catalog scalar carriers in an existing schema; other source obligations require residuals or strict refusal.",
    "Unspecified emits no availability constraint. Native-only import can observe absent-allowed but cannot recover unspecified authorship; the retained projection receipt recovers it.",
    "Single present-value probes per carrier do not establish scalar value-domain, width, exactness or cross-system type equivalence.",
    "Receipts prove reproducibility, not capture authenticity or live server enforcement; any subsequent change requires renewed verification.",
    "Two priority bindings now have qualified evidence; the experimental core and remaining three bindings still need the Nullability delivery gate. No native concept replacement is claimed."
  ],
